# Phase 1.1 — Structural Hardening Plan (Revised per Strategic Review)

## 1. Database Schema Hardening

#### [MODIFY] [database.service.ts](file:///c:/Users/psbon/Telecombank%20App/backend/src/database/database.service.ts)

Apply the following auto-migrations to clean and enforce the schema:

**Users Table (Identity)**
```sql
ALTER TABLE users ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS full_name VARCHAR(100);
ALTER TABLE users ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS updated_at TIMESTAMP DEFAULT NOW();

-- Add trigger for real updated_at
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION update_updated_at_column()
RETURNS TRIGGER AS $$
BEGIN
   NEW.updated_at = NOW();
   RETURN NEW;
END;
$$ language 'plpgsql';

DROP TRIGGER IF EXISTS update_users_updated_at ON users;
CREATE TRIGGER update_users_updated_at
BEFORE UPDATE ON users
FOR EACH ROW EXECUTE FUNCTION update_updated_at_column();
```

**Businesses Table (1:1 Enforcement)**
```sql
ALTER TABLE businesses ADD CONSTRAINT unique_user_business UNIQUE (user_id);
```
*(Backend logic will auto-create 1 default business per user registration).*

**Transactions Table (Minimalist)**
```diff
KEEP: id, user_id, amount, type, category_id, transaction_date, created_at
ADD:  business_id UUID REFERENCES businesses(id)
ADD:  description VARCHAR(255)
ADD:  updated_at TIMESTAMP DEFAULT NOW()
ADD:  deleted_at TIMESTAMP NULL
DROP: source, category, note
DROP: status, provider_reference, idempotency_key, payment_method (Unused/Premature)
```
*(Will also add the `updated_at` trigger to transactions).*

**Categories Table**
```sql
ALTER TABLE categories ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS is_system BOOLEAN DEFAULT FALSE;
```
*(Seed all 10 system categories with `is_system = true`, see previous plan for list).*

**Indexes**
```sql
CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_categories_is_system ON categories(is_system);
CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_transactions_user_date ON transactions(user_id, transaction_date DESC);
CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_transactions_business_date ON transactions(business_id, transaction_date DESC);
```

